IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gp-dates`

-- Supreme Court Act 1986 (Vic), Part 4A (group proceeding, ss 33A-33ZK) -- the rules, shared by both seats.
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in gp-seat.l4 (the group member) and gp-seat-plaintiff.l4 (the
-- representative plaintiff), which IMPORT it and never restate a rule. Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Part's own words say no ("does not apply", "may not be
-- commenced", "is not a group member unless", "may not order", "must not be made unless", "may only", "before the date so
-- fixed", "within a further 21 days", an "if" condition that fails); or NOTHING where the Part does not answer on the facts
-- given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. The Court's judgments ("satisfied", "thinks fit", "just", leave, approval) are
-- inputs: the answer is conditional on them, never a guess at them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Supreme Court
-- Act 1986, Version No. 113 (15 April 2026), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with the
-- authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with the
-- Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Part 4A -- Group proceeding`

§§ `Divisions 1 and 2 -- when a group proceeding may be brought (ss 33B, 33C, 33D, 33G)`

-- s 33B(2): "This Part does not apply to -- (a) a proceeding under sections 34 and 35 of the Act; or (b) a proceeding
-- concerning -- (i) the administration of the estate of a deceased person; or (ii) property subject to a trust; or (c) a
-- proceeding commenced under Order 18 of Chapter I of the Rules."
DECLARE `Kind of proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `a claim of any other kind`
    `a proceeding under sections 34 and 35`
    `a proceeding concerning the administration of the estate of a deceased person`
    `a proceeding concerning property subject to a trust`
    `a proceeding commenced under Order 18 of Chapter I of the Rules`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of proceeding`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 4A applies to` `the kind` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a claim of any other kind` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 33C(1): "Subject to this Part, if -- (a) seven or more persons have claims against the same person; and (b) the claims of
-- all those persons are in respect of, or arise out of, the same, similar or related circumstances; and (c) the claims of all
-- those persons give rise to a substantial common question of law or fact -- a proceeding may be commenced by one or more of
-- those persons as representing some or all of them." s 33C(2): whatever the relief (equitable relief, damages, damages
-- needing individual assessment, relief not the same for each person) and whether or not separate contracts or separate
-- acts are involved -- so the kind of relief is not asked.
-- s 33G: "A group proceeding may not be commenced if the proceeding would be concerned only with claims in respect of which
-- the Court has jurisdiction solely by virtue of the Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 or a corresponding law".
GIVEN `the number of persons with claims against the same person` IS A NUMBER
      `the claims arise out of the same, similar or related circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claims give rise to a substantial common question of law or fact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind` IS A `Kind of proceeding`
      `the Court's jurisdiction over every claim is solely by cross-vesting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33C -- a group proceeding may be commenced` `the number of persons with claims against the same person` `the claims arise out of the same, similar or related circumstances` `the claims give rise to a substantial common question of law or fact` `the kind` `the Court's jurisdiction over every claim is solely by cross-vesting` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`Part 4A applies to` `the kind`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the Court's jurisdiction over every claim is solely by cross-vesting` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF     `the number of persons with claims against the same person` AT LEAST 7
              AND `the claims arise out of the same, similar or related circumstances`
              AND `the claims give rise to a substantial common question of law or fact`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 33D(1): a person within s 33C(1)(a) "who has a sufficient interest to commence a proceeding on the person's own behalf
-- against another person has a sufficient interest to commence a group proceeding against that other person on behalf of
-- other persons referred to in that paragraph." Sufficient interest on one's own behalf is a borrowed (general law) term:
-- asked. Where it is lacking, s 33D(1) gives no standing; the Part is silent on whether anything else could (NOTHING).
GIVEN `the proceeding may be commenced` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `I am one of the persons with claims` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have a sufficient interest to sue the defendant on my own behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33D -- I may commence it as representative` `the proceeding may be commenced` `I am one of the persons with claims` `I have a sufficient interest to sue the defendant on my own behalf` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the proceeding may be commenced`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `I am one of the persons with claims`
        THEN IF `I have a sufficient interest to sue the defendant on my own behalf`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 33D(1) gives standing from a sufficient interest on one's own behalf, and says nothing of other routes)
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- s 33C(1): "by one or more of those persons"
    OTHERWISE `the proceeding may be commenced`

-- s 33D(2): "If a person has commenced a group proceeding, that person retains a sufficient interest -- (a) to continue the
-- proceeding; and (b) to bring an appeal from a judgment in the proceeding -- even though the person ceases to have a claim
-- against the defendant." A plaintiff substituted under s 33T(1) or s 33W(3) did not commence it: s 33D(2) is silent for
-- them (finding 3).
GIVEN `I commenced the group proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33D(2) -- I keep standing after my own claim ends` `I commenced the group proceeding` MEANS
    IF `I commenced the group proceeding`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: "If a person has commenced"; a substituted plaintiff is not mentioned)

§§ `Division 2 -- who is a group member (ss 33A, 33E, 33F, 33J, 33K, 33KA)`

-- s 33A: "group member means a member of a group of persons on whose behalf a group proceeding has been commenced".
-- s 33E(1): "the consent of a person to be a group member is not required." s 33E(2): "None of the following persons is a
-- group member unless the person gives consent in writing to being so -- (a) the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; (b) a
-- Minister ...; (c) a body corporate established for a public purpose by a law ..., other than an incorporated company or
-- association; (d) any judge, magistrate or other judicial officer ...; (e) any other officer ..., in his or her capacity as an
-- officer." s 33J(2): a group member "may opt out ... by notice in writing before the date so fixed"; (6): the Court may
-- reinstate a person who opted out. s 33KA(1): the Court may order "that a person cease to be a group member" or "not become
-- a group member".
GIVEN `I fall within the group the writ describes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a government, Minister, public body, judicial officer or officer acting as such` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have consented in writing to be a group member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have opted out` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has reinstated me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has ordered under s 33KA that I cease to be or not become a group member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33A, 33E -- I am a group member` `I fall within the group the writ describes` `I am a government, Minister, public body, judicial officer or officer acting as such` `I have consented in writing to be a group member` `I have opted out` `the Court has reinstated me` `the Court has ordered under s 33KA that I cease to be or not become a group member` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `I fall within the group the writ describes` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `I am a government, Minister, public body, judicial officer or officer acting as such` AND (NOT `I have consented in writing to be a group member`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the Court has ordered under s 33KA that I cease to be or not become a group member` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `I have opted out` AND (NOT `the Court has reinstated me`) THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 33J(1), (2): "The Court must fix a date before which a group member may opt out"; "A group member may opt out of the
-- group proceeding by notice in writing before the date so fixed." (3): the Court may extend the period. The date is the one
-- fixed, as extended.
GIVEN `the date fixed for opting out` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 33J(2) -- the last day to opt out` `the date fixed for opting out` MEANS `the date` (0 MINUS 1) `days after` `the date fixed for opting out`

GIVEN `the date fixed for opting out` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33J(2) -- I may opt out today` `the date fixed for opting out` `today` MEANS
    IF `today` `is before` `the date fixed for opting out`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 33K(1), (2): with leave, the plaintiff may amend the writ so that the group includes a person "(a) whose cause of action
-- accrued after the commencement of the group proceeding but before such date as the Court fixes when giving leave; and (b)
-- who would have been included in the group ... if the cause of action had accrued before the commencement". Without leave
-- the description is not altered (fork F3).
GIVEN `the Court has given leave to alter the group under s 33K` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day my cause of action accrued` IS A DATE
      `the day the group proceeding was commenced` IS A DATE
      `the date the Court fixed when giving leave` IS A DATE
      `I would have been in the group had my cause of action accrued earlier` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33K -- the group may be altered to include me` `the Court has given leave to alter the group under s 33K` `the day my cause of action accrued` `the day the group proceeding was commenced` `the date the Court fixed when giving leave` `I would have been in the group had my cause of action accrued earlier` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the day my cause of action accrued` `is after` `the day the group proceeding was commenced`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 33K is for causes of action accruing after commencement)
           IF NOT `the Court has given leave to alter the group under s 33K` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF NOT (`the day my cause of action accrued` `is before` `the date the Court fixed when giving leave`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF NOT `I would have been in the group had my cause of action accrued earlier` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 33F: "(1) It is not necessary for a person under disability to have a litigation guardian merely in order to be a group
-- member. (2) A group member who is a person under disability may only take a step in the group proceeding, or conduct part of
-- the proceeding, by the group member's litigation guardian." s 33A: "person under disability means a minor or handicapped
-- person"; "handicapped person means a person who is incapable by reason of injury, disease, senility, illness or physical
-- or mental infirmity of managing his or her affairs in relation to the proceeding". "Minor" is borrowed: asked as under 18.
GIVEN `I am under 18` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am incapable of managing my affairs in the proceeding because of injury, disease, senility, illness or infirmity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 33A -- I am a person under disability` `I am under 18` `I am incapable of managing my affairs in the proceeding because of injury, disease, senility, illness or infirmity` IF
    `I am under 18` OR `I am incapable of managing my affairs in the proceeding because of injury, disease, senility, illness or infirmity`

GIVEN `I am a person under disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I want to take a step or conduct part of the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33F -- I must act by a litigation guardian` `I am a person under disability` `I want to take a step or conduct part of the proceeding` MEANS
    IF `I am a person under disability`
    THEN IF `I want to take a step or conduct part of the proceeding`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 33F speaks only of persons under disability)

§§ `Division 6 -- costs (ss 33Q(3), 33R(2), 33ZD, 33ZDA, 33ZJ)`

-- s 33ZD(1): the Court "(a) may order the plaintiff or the defendant to pay costs; (b) except as authorised by section 33Q or
-- 33R, may not order a group member or a sub-group member to pay costs." (2): "(1)(b) is subject to any order made under
-- section 33ZDA." s 33Q(3): a sub-group representative party other than the plaintiff, "and not the plaintiff, is liable for
-- costs associated with the determination of the question or questions common to the sub-group members". s 33R(2): an
-- individual group member permitted to take part on a question only about their own claim, "and not the plaintiff, is liable
-- for costs associated with the determination of the question". s 33ZDA(1)(b): under a group costs order "liability for
-- payment of the legal costs must be shared among the plaintiff and all group members".
DECLARE `Costs a group member can be made to pay` IS ONE OF
    `the costs of deciding the sub-group's common questions, as sub-group representative party (s 33Q(3))`
    `the costs of deciding the question that relates only to my claim (s 33R(2))`
    `a share of the legal costs of the law practice under the group costs order (s 33ZDA(1)(b))`

GIVEN `I am a sub-group representative party and not the plaintiff` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I take part to decide a question only about my own claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a group costs order is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Costs a group member can be made to pay`
`s 33ZD -- the costs I can be made to pay as a group member` `I am a sub-group representative party and not the plaintiff` `I take part to decide a question only about my own claim` `a group costs order is in force` MEANS
    concat (LIST `the sub-group costs`, `the individual costs`, `the group costs order share`)
    WHERE
        `the sub-group costs` MEANS
            IF `I am a sub-group representative party and not the plaintiff`
            THEN LIST `the costs of deciding the sub-group's common questions, as sub-group representative party (s 33Q(3))`
            ELSE EMPTY
        `the individual costs` MEANS
            IF `I take part to decide a question only about my own claim`
            THEN LIST `the costs of deciding the question that relates only to my claim (s 33R(2))`
            ELSE EMPTY
        `the group costs order share` MEANS
            IF `a group costs order is in force`
            THEN LIST `a share of the legal costs of the law practice under the group costs order (s 33ZDA(1)(b))`
            ELSE EMPTY

-- s 33ZDA(1): "On application by the plaintiff in any group proceeding, the Court, if satisfied that it is appropriate or
-- necessary to ensure that justice is done in the proceeding, may make an order -- (a) that the legal costs payable to the
-- law practice representing the plaintiff and group members be calculated as a percentage of the amount of any award or
-- settlement that may be recovered in the proceeding, being the percentage set out in the order; and (b) that liability for
-- payment of the legal costs must be shared among the plaintiff and all group members." Without an application, no power
-- (fork F4).
GIVEN `the plaintiff has applied for a group costs order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied it is appropriate or necessary to ensure justice is done` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33ZDA(1) -- the Court may make a group costs order` `the plaintiff has applied for a group costs order` `the Court is satisfied it is appropriate or necessary to ensure justice is done` MEANS
    IF `the plaintiff has applied for a group costs order` AND `the Court is satisfied it is appropriate or necessary to ensure justice is done`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 33ZDA(1)(a), (3): the legal costs are the percentage in the order (as amended) of the amount recovered. The percentage is
-- the Court's: an input. With no group costs order the legal costs are fixed under the Legal Profession Uniform Law
-- (Victoria) and the costs agreement, outside this Act: NOTHING.
GIVEN `a group costs order is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the percentage in the order` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the award or settlement recovered` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 33ZDA(1)(a) -- the legal costs under the group costs order` `a group costs order is in force` `the percentage in the order` `the amount of the award or settlement recovered` MEANS
    IF `a group costs order is in force`
    THEN JUST ((`the amount of the award or settlement recovered` TIMES `the percentage in the order`) DIVIDED BY 100)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: the Legal Profession Uniform Law (Victoria) and the costs agreement)

-- s 33ZDA(1)(b): the liability is "shared among the plaintiff and all group members", without saying in what shares. The
-- encoding computes one person's share only where the order itself shares the costs in proportion to each person's recovery
-- (fork F5); otherwise the order's own terms decide: NOTHING.
DECLARE `My share under a group costs order` HAS
    `the legal costs I bear` IS A NUMBER
    `what I keep` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `a group costs order is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the percentage in the order` IS A NUMBER
      `the order shares the costs in proportion to each person's recovery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount I recover` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `My share under a group costs order`
`s 33ZDA(1)(b) -- my share under the group costs order` `a group costs order is in force` `the percentage in the order` `the order shares the costs in proportion to each person's recovery` `the amount I recover` MEANS
    IF `a group costs order is in force`
    THEN IF `the order shares the costs in proportion to each person's recovery`
         THEN JUST (`My share under a group costs order` WITH
                        `the legal costs I bear` IS `my costs`
                        `what I keep`            IS `the amount I recover` MINUS `my costs`)
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 33ZDA(1)(b) says "shared" but not in what shares; the order's terms decide)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: without a group costs order, s 33ZDA does not apply)
    WHERE
        `my costs` MEANS (`the amount I recover` TIMES `the percentage in the order`) DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 33ZD(1)(a) and s 33ZDA(2): who answers for the defendant's costs. "If a group costs order is made -- (a) the law practice
-- representing the plaintiff and group members is liable to pay any costs payable to the defendant in the proceeding; and
-- (b) the law practice ... must give any security for the costs of the defendant in the proceeding that the Court may order
-- the plaintiff to give." Whether the plaintiff stays liable beside the law practice is not said (finding 4).
DECLARE `Who answers for the defendant's costs` IS ONE OF
    `the plaintiff, if the Court so orders (s 33ZD(1)(a))`
    `the law practice representing the plaintiff and group members, which must also give any security for costs ordered (s 33ZDA(2))`

GIVEN `a group costs order is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Who answers for the defendant's costs`
`s 33ZD, 33ZDA(2) -- who answers for the defendant's costs` `a group costs order is in force` MEANS
    IF `a group costs order is in force`
    THEN `the law practice representing the plaintiff and group members, which must also give any security for costs ordered (s 33ZDA(2))`
    ELSE `the plaintiff, if the Court so orders (s 33ZD(1)(a))`

-- s 33ZJ: "(1) If the Court has made an award of damages in a group proceeding, the plaintiff or a sub-group representative
-- party, or a person who has been a plaintiff or such a party, may apply ... (2) If ... the Court is satisfied that the costs
-- reasonably incurred in relation to the group proceeding by the person making the application are likely to exceed the
-- costs recoverable by the person from the defendant, the Court may order that an amount equal to the whole or a part of the
-- excess be paid to that person out of the damages awarded." The most is the whole excess; 0 where no order can be made.
GIVEN `the Court has made an award of damages` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied the costs reasonably incurred are likely to exceed those recoverable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs reasonably incurred` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs recoverable from the defendant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 33ZJ -- the most that may be paid out of the damages for the representative's costs` `the Court has made an award of damages` `the Court is satisfied the costs reasonably incurred are likely to exceed those recoverable` `the costs reasonably incurred` `the costs recoverable from the defendant` MEANS
    IF `the Court has made an award of damages` AND `the Court is satisfied the costs reasonably incurred are likely to exceed those recoverable`
    THEN max 0 (`the costs reasonably incurred` MINUS `the costs recoverable from the defendant`)
    ELSE 0

§§ `Division 6 -- limitation periods (s 33ZE)`

-- s 33ZE: "(1) Upon the commencement of a group proceeding, the running of any limitation period that applies to the claim of a
-- group member to which the proceeding relates is suspended. (2) The limitation period does not begin to run again unless
-- either the member opts out of the proceeding under section 33J or the proceeding, and any appeals arising from the
-- proceeding, are determined without finally disposing of the group member's claim."
-- The days from the commencement to the day it runs again are added to the last day (fork F6). s 33J(5) ("must be taken
-- never to have been a group member") is read as not undoing the suspension, since s 33ZE(2) speaks of the member who opts
-- out (finding 2). The limitation period itself is outside this Act (Limitation of Actions Act 1958, not deposited): the
-- last day it gives is asked.
DECLARE `My limitation period` IS ONE OF
    `not suspended by s 33ZE: my claim is not one the group proceeding relates to`
    `it had already ended before the group proceeding was commenced`
    `suspended, and not yet running again (s 33ZE(2))`
    `running again (s 33ZE(2)), with a new last day` HAS `the new last day` IS A DATE

GIVEN `my claim is one the group proceeding relates to` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the group proceeding was commenced` IS A DATE
      `the last day I could have sued had there been no group proceeding` IS A DATE
      `I have opted out` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I opted out` IS A DATE
      `the proceeding and appeals ended without finally disposing of my claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day they ended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `My limitation period`
`s 33ZE -- my limitation period` `my claim is one the group proceeding relates to` `the day the group proceeding was commenced` `the last day I could have sued had there been no group proceeding` `I have opted out` `the day I opted out` `the proceeding and appeals ended without finally disposing of my claim` `the day they ended` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `my claim is one the group proceeding relates to` THEN `not suspended by s 33ZE: my claim is not one the group proceeding relates to`
           IF `the last day I could have sued had there been no group proceeding` `is before` `the day the group proceeding was commenced` THEN `it had already ended before the group proceeding was commenced`
           IF `I have opted out` THEN `running again (s 33ZE(2)), with a new last day` (`the new last day from` `the day I opted out`)
           IF `the proceeding and appeals ended without finally disposing of my claim` THEN `running again (s 33ZE(2)), with a new last day` (`the new last day from` `the day they ended`)
           OTHERWISE `suspended, and not yet running again (s 33ZE(2))`
    WHERE
        GIVEN `the day it runs again` IS A DATE
        GIVETH A DATE
        `the new last day from` `the day it runs again` MEANS
            `the date` (`the days from` `the day the group proceeding was commenced` `to` `the day it runs again`) `days after` `the last day I could have sued had there been no group proceeding`

§§ `Divisions 4 and 6 -- steps and claims by a date (ss 33ZA(3), (4), 33ZG)`

DECLARE `Member party` IS ONE OF
    `the group member`

DECLARE `Member act` IS ONE OF
    `take the step the order sets out`
    `make a claim for payment out of the fund`

-- s 33ZG: an order under s 33ZF may "(a) set out a step that group members or a specified class of group members must take to
-- be entitled to -- (i) any relief under section 33Z; or (ii) any payment out of a fund constituted under section 33ZA; or
-- (iii) obtain any other benefit arising out of the proceeding -- ... (b) specify a date after which, if the step ... has not
-- been taken by a group member to whom the order applies, the group member is not entitled to any relief or payment or to
-- obtain any other benefit". The step may be taken on the date itself; the rule runs on plain days from the order.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Member party` `Member act`
`s 33ZG -- the group member must take the step by the date` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the group member`
    MUST `take the step the order sets out`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the group member` BECAUSE "the step was not taken by the date: the group member is not entitled to the relief, payment or benefit (s 33ZG(b))"

-- s 33ZA(3)(c): the order constituting a fund must "specify a day (which is 6 months or more after the day on which the order
-- is made) on or before which the group members are to make a claim for payment out of the fund". (4): "The Court may, if it
-- is just, allow a group member to make a claim after the day fixed under subsection (3)(c) if the fund has not already been
-- fully distributed."
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Member party` `Member act`
`s 33ZA(3)(c) -- the group member is to claim from the fund by the day fixed` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the group member`
    MUST `make a claim for payment out of the fund`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the group member` BECAUSE "no claim on or before the day fixed: a later claim only if the Court allows it as just and the fund is not fully distributed (s 33ZA(4))"

-- The helper that runs a duty over what happened (as in the Accident Compensation Act 1985 encoding, aca-damages.l4). On the
-- stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: where the act was done, FULFILLED means in time and
-- anything else late; where it was not, the helper asks whether doing it now would still be in time. It takes a DEONTIC
-- value, so it is never exported.
DECLARE `What became of the step` IS ONE OF
    `done in time`
    `not done in time`
    `still open`

GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Member party` `Member act`
      `the act` IS A `Member act`
      `the act has been done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time the act was done` IS A NUMBER
      `the time now` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What became of the step`
`what became of` `the rule` `with` `the act` `done` `the act has been done` `at` `the time the act was done` `now` `the time now` MEANS
    IF `the act has been done`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time the act was done`), (EVENT `the group member` `the act` `the time the act was done`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `done in time`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time now`), (EVENT `the group member` `the act` `the time now`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still open`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`

GIVEN `the day of the order` IS A DATE
      `the date the order specifies` IS A DATE
      `I have taken the step` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I took the step` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `What became of the step`
`s 33ZG -- what became of my step` `the day of the order` `the date the order specifies` `I have taken the step` `the day I took the step` `today` MEANS
    `what became of` (`s 33ZG -- the group member must take the step by the date` (`the days from` `the day of the order` `to` `the date the order specifies`)) `with` `take the step the order sets out` `done` `I have taken the step` `at` (`the days from` `the day of the order` `to` `the day I took the step`) `now` (`the days from` `the day of the order` `to` `today`)

-- s 33ZA(3)(c): the earliest day the order may fix is 6 months after the order (fork F7 for a day the later month lacks).
GIVEN `the day of the order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 33ZA(3)(c) -- the earliest day the order may fix for claims` `the day of the order` MEANS `the date` 6 `months after` `the day of the order`

GIVEN `the day of the order` IS A DATE
      `the day fixed for claims` IS A DATE
      `I have made my claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I made my claim` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
      `the fund has been fully distributed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court allows my late claim as just` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33ZA(3)(c), (4) -- my claim on the fund is in time or allowed` `the day of the order` `the day fixed for claims` `I have made my claim` `the day I made my claim` `today` `the fund has been fully distributed` `the Court allows my late claim as just` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what became of` (`s 33ZA(3)(c) -- the group member is to claim from the fund by the day fixed` (`the days from` `the day of the order` `to` `the day fixed for claims`)) `with` `make a claim for payment out of the fund` `done` `I have made my claim` `at` (`the days from` `the day of the order` `to` `the day I made my claim`) `now` (`the days from` `the day of the order` `to` `today`)
    WHEN `done in time` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `still open` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `not done in time` THEN
        IF `the fund has been fully distributed`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE IF `the Court allows my late claim as just`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Division 3 -- notices (ss 33X, 33Y)`

-- s 33X(1): "Notice must be given to group members of ... (a) the commencement of the proceeding and the right of the group
-- members to opt out ...; (b) an application by the defendant for the dismissal of the proceeding on the ground of want of
-- prosecution; (c) an application by the plaintiff seeking leave under section 33W." (2): "The Court may dispense with
-- compliance with any or all of the requirements of subsection (1) if the relief sought in a proceeding does not include any
-- claim for damages." (3): "If the Court so orders, notice must be given to group members of any offer to compromise the
-- proceeding." (4): "Unless the Court is satisfied that it is just to do so, an application for approval under section 33V
-- must not be determined unless notice has been given to group members." (5): "The Court may, at any stage, order that
-- notice of any matter be given". (6): "as soon as practicable after the happening of the event".
DECLARE `Matter for notice` IS ONE OF
    `the commencement of the proceeding and my right to opt out`
    `the defendant's application to dismiss for want of prosecution`
    `the plaintiff's application for leave under s 33W to settle the plaintiff's own claim`
    `an offer to compromise the proceeding`
    `an application for the Court's approval of a settlement or discontinuance`
    `any other matter`

GIVEN `the matter` IS A `Matter for notice`
      `the relief sought includes a claim for damages` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has dispensed with notice of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has ordered notice of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied it is just to decide the approval without notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33X -- notice of the matter must be given to me` `the matter` `the relief sought includes a claim for damages` `the Court has dispensed with notice of it` `the Court has ordered notice of it` `the Court is satisfied it is just to decide the approval without notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `an offer to compromise the proceeding` THEN
        IF `the Court has ordered notice of it` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an application for the Court's approval of a settlement or discontinuance` THEN
        IF `the Court is satisfied it is just to decide the approval without notice` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `any other matter` THEN
        IF `the Court has ordered notice of it`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 33X(5) is a power to order notice, and without an order the Part says nothing)
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the Court has dispensed with notice of it` AND (NOT `the relief sought includes a claim for damages`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Divisions 4 and 5 -- judgment and appeals (ss 33ZB, 33ZC(5))`

-- s 33ZB: "A judgment given in a group proceeding -- (a) must describe or otherwise identify the group members who will be
-- affected by it; and (b) subject to section 33KA, binds all persons who are such group members at the time the judgment is
-- given." s 33KA(3): if the Court so orders, a person who ceases to be a group member "must be taken never to have been" one.
GIVEN `I was a group member when the judgment was given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has since ordered under s 33KA that I cease to be a group member and am taken never to have been one` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33ZB -- the judgment binds me` `I was a group member when the judgment was given` `the Court has since ordered under s 33KA that I cease to be a group member and am taken never to have been one` MEANS
    IF `I was a group member when the judgment was given`
    THEN IF `the Court has since ordered under s 33KA that I cease to be a group member and am taken never to have been one`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 33ZB says whom the judgment binds, not whom it does not)

-- s 33ZC(5): "If the plaintiff or the sub-group representative party does not commence an appeal within the time provided,
-- another member of the group or sub-group may, within a further 21 days, commence an appeal as representing the group members
-- or sub-group members". The time provided is set by the rules of court (not deposited): asked as its last day. While it is
-- still running the condition is not yet met (fork F8).
GIVEN `the last day of the time provided for the representative's appeal` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 33ZC(5) -- the last day I may appeal as representative` `the last day of the time provided for the representative's appeal` MEANS `the date` 21 `days after` `the last day of the time provided for the representative's appeal`

GIVEN `the last day of the time provided for the representative's appeal` IS A DATE
      `the representative has commenced an appeal in time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33ZC(5) -- I may appeal as representative today` `the last day of the time provided for the representative's appeal` `the representative has commenced an appeal in time` `today` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the representative has commenced an appeal in time` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF NOT (`today` `is after` `the last day of the time provided for the representative's appeal`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `today` `is after` (`s 33ZC(5) -- the last day I may appeal as representative` `the last day of the time provided for the representative's appeal`) THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Division 2 -- settlement and leaving Part 4A (ss 33P, 33V, 33W)`

-- s 33V(1): "A group proceeding may not be settled or discontinued without the approval of the Court."
GIVEN `the Court has approved the settlement or discontinuance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33V -- the group proceeding may be settled or discontinued` `the Court has approved the settlement or discontinuance` MEANS
    IF `the Court has approved the settlement or discontinuance` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 33W(1): "The plaintiff may, with the leave of the Court, settle the plaintiff's individual claim in whole or in part at any
-- stage of the group proceeding."
GIVEN `the Court has given leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33W(1) -- I may settle my individual claim` `the Court has given leave` MEANS
    IF `the Court has given leave` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 33W(2), (4): the Court may order that a plaintiff who has settled cease to be plaintiff, but "An order must not be made
-- under subsection (2) unless the Court is satisfied that -- (a) notice of application for the order has been given to group
-- members in accordance with section 33X(1); and (b) such notice was given in sufficient time for an application to be made
-- for an order under subsection (3); and (c) an order under subsection (3) has been or will be made." Each is asked as the
-- Court's finding.
GIVEN `I have settled my individual claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied notice of the application was given to group members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied it was given in time for a substitution application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied a substitute plaintiff has been or will be ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33W(2), (4) -- I may be ordered to cease to be plaintiff` `I have settled my individual claim` `the Court is satisfied notice of the application was given to group members` `the Court is satisfied it was given in time for a substitution application` `the Court is satisfied a substitute plaintiff has been or will be ordered` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `I have settled my individual claim` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 33W(2) is about a person who has settled)
           IF     `the Court is satisfied notice of the application was given to group members`
              AND `the Court is satisfied it was given in time for a substitution application`
              AND `the Court is satisfied a substitute plaintiff has been or will be ordered`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 33P: "If the Court makes an order under section 33L, 33M or 33N that a proceeding no longer continue under this Part -- (a)
-- the proceeding may be continued as a proceeding by the plaintiff on the plaintiff's own behalf against the defendant; and
-- (b) on the application of a person who was a group member, the Court may order that the person be joined as a plaintiff".
GIVEN `the Court has ordered under s 33L, 33M or 33N that it no longer continue under Part 4A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33P(a) -- I may continue on my own behalf` `the Court has ordered under s 33L, 33M or 33N that it no longer continue under Part 4A` MEANS
    IF `the Court has ordered under s 33L, 33M or 33N that it no longer continue under Part 4A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 33P speaks only after such an order)
